WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.387
Here are the nine rules
the planner applies.

2
00:00:02.387 --> 00:00:06.457
Before any of them, it reads
each app registration, identity,

3
00:00:06.457 --> 00:00:11.688
role assignment and legacy account, plus
sign-ins once a cutover is recorded.

4
00:00:11.688 --> 00:00:16.917
Most rules come straight from Learn: the
subject, issuer and audience must match

5
00:00:16.917 --> 00:00:22.225
exactly, names must follow the rules, and
no parent may go past twenty credentials.

6
00:00:22.225 --> 00:00:26.936
Three are the program's own and labeled
that way: the conversion order, a warning

7
00:00:26.936 --> 00:00:31.575
for credentials nobody reviewed, and
the thresholds for a clean parallel run.

8
00:00:31.575 --> 00:00:34.510
And the failed exchange
test is its own finding.
